01:05:36.150 --> 01:05:38.280
So it's a great pleasure
for me to be here.

01:05:38.280 --> 01:05:41.340
I've recently moved
to Europe from the US,

01:05:41.340 --> 01:05:44.520
from Mountain View, to
run our sales engineering,

01:05:44.520 --> 01:05:47.250
pre-sales engineering
organization across AMEA.

01:05:47.250 --> 01:05:49.620
And we're making huge
investments in this.

01:05:49.620 --> 01:05:52.770
Because if we're going to
activate security, secure

01:05:52.770 --> 01:05:54.690
applications, and
secure development,

01:05:54.690 --> 01:05:56.850
if we're going to bring
artificial intelligence

01:05:56.850 --> 01:05:58.734
and machine learning
to the applications

01:05:58.734 --> 01:06:00.900
that you're building, we
need to have an engineering

01:06:00.900 --> 01:06:03.300
team in AMEA that
you can partner with,

01:06:03.300 --> 01:06:05.100
that you can spend
time with and be

01:06:05.100 --> 01:06:07.020
able to interact
to be able to build

01:06:07.020 --> 01:06:10.402
the next set of applications
on top of this infrastructure.

01:06:10.402 --> 01:06:11.860
I want to spend a
couple of minutes

01:06:11.860 --> 01:06:15.090
this morning bringing in
another component of the suite

01:06:15.090 --> 01:06:17.100
that we have around
Google Cloud.

01:06:17.100 --> 01:06:19.560
And the suite that we're
introducing, or actually have

01:06:19.560 --> 01:06:23.070
been working on for some time
is our collaboration suite.

01:06:23.070 --> 01:06:24.300
And we've had great success.

01:06:24.300 --> 01:06:26.590
And you can see by
the numbers, right,

01:06:26.590 --> 01:06:30.750
that there are great accolades
for the power of G Suite

01:06:30.750 --> 01:06:32.640
and what it's doing
to help organizations

01:06:32.640 --> 01:06:36.972
begin to connect, collaborate,
and create the next big idea.

01:06:36.972 --> 01:06:38.430
And we can run
through the numbers.

01:06:38.430 --> 01:06:42.060
We've been at this for a
little over 10 years now.

01:06:42.060 --> 01:06:44.130
I actually have been
here at Google coming up

01:06:44.130 --> 01:06:45.990
on 10 years in September.

01:06:45.990 --> 01:06:51.030
We have over a billion seven-day
active users over three

01:06:51.030 --> 01:06:52.410
of the application areas.

01:06:52.410 --> 01:06:55.680
And we have over 3
million customers

01:06:55.680 --> 01:06:58.744
that are using these
applications on a daily basis.

01:06:58.744 --> 01:07:00.660
But the important question
that I have for you

01:07:00.660 --> 01:07:04.150
today is not how successful
it's been in the past.

01:07:04.150 --> 01:07:07.600
The most important question is
why has this been successful?

01:07:07.600 --> 01:07:10.740
Why are we seeing the
adoption within Google

01:07:10.740 --> 01:07:12.270
of these applications?

01:07:12.270 --> 01:07:13.920
And what I would
submit to you is

01:07:13.920 --> 01:07:16.170
it's all about the
creative process.

01:07:16.170 --> 01:07:20.070
I had the opportunity this last
weekend to attend a graduation

01:07:20.070 --> 01:07:22.590
ceremony for my
youngest daughter.

01:07:22.590 --> 01:07:24.000
So I have five kids.

01:07:24.000 --> 01:07:26.190
And my youngest
daughter Kelly recently

01:07:26.190 --> 01:07:29.880
graduated from the Savannah
College of Art and Design.

01:07:29.880 --> 01:07:31.350
It's in Savannah, Georgia.

01:07:31.350 --> 01:07:34.260
It's a school that's dedicated
to the creative arts,

01:07:34.260 --> 01:07:39.220
architecture, video-in-motion,
collaboration, fashion--

01:07:39.220 --> 01:07:41.220
which is the area that
my daughter graduated in.

01:07:41.220 --> 01:07:45.540
And at this graduation ceremony,
the president of the school

01:07:45.540 --> 01:07:50.509
stood up and said, in order to
facilitate the next big idea.

01:07:50.509 --> 01:07:52.050
If you think about
what you're trying

01:07:52.050 --> 01:07:55.470
to do to transform business,
to transform your customers,

01:07:55.470 --> 01:07:58.380
to transform the services
that you're providing,

01:07:58.380 --> 01:08:00.930
you have to create
that next big idea.

01:08:00.930 --> 01:08:05.040
That creation comes
from the ability

01:08:05.040 --> 01:08:09.390
to be able to think of new
10x thinking ideas, which

01:08:09.390 --> 01:08:12.720
comes from creative
applications and being

01:08:12.720 --> 01:08:14.730
able to actually
create to do that.

01:08:14.730 --> 01:08:18.240
But what is the synthesis, or
the catalyst, or the beginning

01:08:18.240 --> 01:08:20.247
of that creative process?

01:08:20.247 --> 01:08:22.080
At Google, we would
argue that the beginning

01:08:22.080 --> 01:08:24.990
of that creative
process is engagement.

01:08:24.990 --> 01:08:27.149
It's when you sit
around the table,

01:08:27.149 --> 01:08:30.930
or in the conference room, or
on a call, or in a video call

01:08:30.930 --> 01:08:33.790
and begin to communicate and
interact with those around you,

01:08:33.790 --> 01:08:37.210
we start to unlock the
energy of creative.

01:08:37.210 --> 01:08:37.710
Right?

01:08:37.710 --> 01:08:39.689
We begin to bring
forth those new ideas

01:08:39.689 --> 01:08:41.220
and those creative ideas.

01:08:41.220 --> 01:08:43.350
In order to do that,
you need a suite

01:08:43.350 --> 01:08:47.430
of applications that are going
to support you in that process.

01:08:47.430 --> 01:08:51.390
So G Suite is composed of a set
of applications that are really

01:08:51.390 --> 01:08:54.210
designed to unlock that
collaboration spirit,

01:08:54.210 --> 01:08:56.550
to be able to get people
to communicate together

01:08:56.550 --> 01:09:00.120
so that they can come up with
10x new ideas, which you can

01:09:00.120 --> 01:09:03.510
then apply to create the
transformations you need

01:09:03.510 --> 01:09:07.350
to drive your business forward.

01:09:07.350 --> 01:09:10.140
To do that, we think
that there's a problem

01:09:10.140 --> 01:09:11.700
that we have to solve.

01:09:11.700 --> 01:09:14.250
If I want to be able to
unlock the creative spirits

01:09:14.250 --> 01:09:16.330
and be able to
get you to engage,

01:09:16.330 --> 01:09:18.749
I have to be able to
solve three problems.

01:09:18.749 --> 01:09:20.790
Number one is I have to
build a set of tools that

01:09:20.790 --> 01:09:22.979
really focus on team
collaboration, not

01:09:22.979 --> 01:09:24.960
individual productivity.

01:09:24.960 --> 01:09:28.859
Number two is I have to be able
to clear space in the calendar

01:09:28.859 --> 01:09:31.350
by making you more
effective and more efficient

01:09:31.350 --> 01:09:34.170
so that you can actually
have room to collaborate.

01:09:34.170 --> 01:09:38.279
And then number three is I have
to infuse these applications

01:09:38.279 --> 01:09:40.710
with the power of artificial
intelligence and machine

01:09:40.710 --> 01:09:44.790
learning so that you can begin
to elevate your productivity

01:09:44.790 --> 01:09:48.000
and work at new levels so
that you have the ability

01:09:48.000 --> 01:09:50.790
to be able to create the next
generation thing using best

01:09:50.790 --> 01:09:53.939
practices and principles of
those people that are experts

01:09:53.939 --> 01:09:56.310
within the industry,
experts around you,

01:09:56.310 --> 01:09:58.200
experts within the
company, and that you're

01:09:58.200 --> 01:10:00.150
actually communicating
and collaborating

01:10:00.150 --> 01:10:02.710
cross-functionally
within an organization,

01:10:02.710 --> 01:10:07.200
within your department, across
departments, across companies,

01:10:07.200 --> 01:10:09.330
with distributors,
with suppliers,

01:10:09.330 --> 01:10:11.590
and with your customers.

01:10:11.590 --> 01:10:14.140
So that's the power of
artificial intelligence.

01:10:14.140 --> 01:10:16.740
How do we actually make that
happen within the collaboration

01:10:16.740 --> 01:10:17.240
suite?

01:10:17.240 --> 01:10:19.230
Let me have-- are
there two examples,

01:10:19.230 --> 01:10:22.020
Bill, that you could give me
today that might illustrate

01:10:22.020 --> 01:10:25.500
what Google is doing to create
the room in the calendar,

01:10:25.500 --> 01:10:28.260
to make me more
effective, and to actually

01:10:28.260 --> 01:10:30.490
help me engage as a team?

01:10:30.490 --> 01:10:31.110
All right.

01:10:31.110 --> 01:10:35.220
So number one is the
content that we're

01:10:35.220 --> 01:10:37.590
going to collaborate
on has to be

01:10:37.590 --> 01:10:40.680
easy to access, easy to
find, and the ability

01:10:40.680 --> 01:10:42.150
to be able to get
together on that.

01:10:42.150 --> 01:10:45.730
And in fact, Google
Drive, all right,

01:10:45.730 --> 01:10:48.550
is the place where
people are collaborating.

01:10:48.550 --> 01:10:50.320
It is the place where
people are putting

01:10:50.320 --> 01:10:52.330
their collaborative documents
so that they can find them

01:10:52.330 --> 01:10:54.790
easily and be able to share
them across these different

01:10:54.790 --> 01:10:57.460
organizations and across
distributors, suppliers,

01:10:57.460 --> 01:10:59.230
and customers.

01:10:59.230 --> 01:11:01.660
And what we've built
into Google Drive

01:11:01.660 --> 01:11:03.940
is this ability to
have quick access.

01:11:03.940 --> 01:11:06.700
So quick access is
all about the ability

01:11:06.700 --> 01:11:09.280
to be able to find what
you need when you need it,

01:11:09.280 --> 01:11:12.520
and to do it quickly so that
you can save that critical time

01:11:12.520 --> 01:11:14.740
and spend more time working
in the collaborative area

01:11:14.740 --> 01:11:17.710
than finding the documents of
interest that you need to do.

01:11:17.710 --> 01:11:21.880
It turns out that over 40% of
the documents that you access

01:11:21.880 --> 01:11:26.320
today in Drive are found
through this capability in Quick

01:11:26.320 --> 01:11:29.710
Access in Drive, which means
you're spending less time going

01:11:29.710 --> 01:11:32.680
through the folder, and the
subfolder, and the subfolder,

01:11:32.680 --> 01:11:34.680
and the subfolder
to find content.

01:11:34.680 --> 01:11:37.540
The content that you need is
immediately available to you

01:11:37.540 --> 01:11:39.790
by a click of a
button, presented

01:11:39.790 --> 01:11:42.887
to you in the very beginning
of your access of Drive.

01:11:42.887 --> 01:11:44.470
The second thing
that we're working on

01:11:44.470 --> 01:11:47.020
is being able to elevate
your productivity.

01:11:47.020 --> 01:11:48.910
This is one example
of something we're

01:11:48.910 --> 01:11:51.160
doing in Google
Sheets called Explore.

01:11:51.160 --> 01:11:52.690
If you haven't used
Explore, I would

01:11:52.690 --> 01:11:56.380
encourage you to do that this
afternoon or do that tomorrow.

01:11:56.380 --> 01:11:58.240
The concept is this.

01:11:58.240 --> 01:12:03.190
Is that unless you are a
sophisticated spreadsheet

01:12:03.190 --> 01:12:06.040
user, writing the
formulas required

01:12:06.040 --> 01:12:10.090
to be able to do complex
queries is a difficult task.

01:12:10.090 --> 01:12:13.270
Why not unlock the power
of artificial intelligence

01:12:13.270 --> 01:12:15.880
and speech recognition
to be able to allow you

01:12:15.880 --> 01:12:18.160
to simply speak your request?

01:12:18.160 --> 01:12:22.450
Show me in the inventory
all of the products

01:12:22.450 --> 01:12:25.150
that have been sold across
these different regions

01:12:25.150 --> 01:12:29.890
within the last seven days,
and show me the highest ticket

01:12:29.890 --> 01:12:31.860
items and the biggest margin.

01:12:31.860 --> 01:12:35.620
What if I could simply just
state that as a question?

01:12:35.620 --> 01:12:40.000
And then Google Sheets would
then interpret that language

01:12:40.000 --> 01:12:42.040
and be able to turn
that into a formula

01:12:42.040 --> 01:12:43.630
and be able to allow
you to visualize

01:12:43.630 --> 01:12:46.330
that content immediately
without having to actually write

01:12:46.330 --> 01:12:47.470
the formula itself.

01:12:47.470 --> 01:12:49.940
And then more importantly, we
actually give you the formula

01:12:49.940 --> 01:12:52.630
that you can then take and
implement in your sheet

01:12:52.630 --> 01:12:55.450
so that the person coming
behind you, the next person

01:12:55.450 --> 01:12:58.360
to go look at this content, can
leverage what you've already

01:12:58.360 --> 01:13:00.850
done in terms of
investigation, and can take

01:13:00.850 --> 01:13:04.210
the power of your thinking,
applied to the spreadsheet,

01:13:04.210 --> 01:13:08.850
with a formula built in
already purposed for you to do.

01:13:08.850 --> 01:13:10.730
But it's more than just
being able to elevate

01:13:10.730 --> 01:13:12.530
your productivity
and be able to allow

01:13:12.530 --> 01:13:14.040
you to work more effectively.

01:13:14.040 --> 01:13:17.480
It's also about being
able to work as a team.

01:13:17.480 --> 01:13:20.330
So today, if you were
to look at the numbers,

01:13:20.330 --> 01:13:22.460
there are over
800 million people

01:13:22.460 --> 01:13:25.820
that are using Google
Drive every single day.

01:13:25.820 --> 01:13:27.590
We're not talking
about registered users.

01:13:27.590 --> 01:13:31.581
We're talking about active
engagement with Google Drive.

01:13:31.581 --> 01:13:33.080
But we didn't think
that was enough.

01:13:33.080 --> 01:13:36.000
Google Drive is a great
platform and a great tool.

01:13:36.000 --> 01:13:38.390
But what we realized is
we need to build something

01:13:38.390 --> 01:13:42.350
for teams, a collaborative space
where you can go and actually

01:13:42.350 --> 01:13:45.560
work with a team, where the
content that you create,

01:13:45.560 --> 01:13:47.450
the information
that you exchange,

01:13:47.450 --> 01:13:49.460
and the work that you're
doing collaboratively

01:13:49.460 --> 01:13:51.600
is available to you immediately.

01:13:51.600 --> 01:13:54.380
And when I come in
as a new team member,

01:13:54.380 --> 01:13:57.140
the team space is persistent.

01:13:57.140 --> 01:13:59.900
Meaning that all the content
that the team has been working

01:13:59.900 --> 01:14:03.080
on up to date is available
to me, and no one on the team

01:14:03.080 --> 01:14:05.660
has to go and share that
information with me.

01:14:05.660 --> 01:14:08.750
It's already available and I
can see what people are doing.

01:14:08.750 --> 01:14:12.860
And then if I leave and go
from Project 1 to Project 2,

01:14:12.860 --> 01:14:15.590
all the content that I
created stays with the team

01:14:15.590 --> 01:14:16.862
in the team space.

01:14:16.862 --> 01:14:18.320
And when I go into
the new project,

01:14:18.320 --> 01:14:19.820
I can immediately
get information

01:14:19.820 --> 01:14:21.069
about what they're working on.

01:14:21.069 --> 01:14:24.890
And I can seamlessly move from
team space, to team space,

01:14:24.890 --> 01:14:27.800
to team space to be able to
collaborate in real time.

01:14:32.600 --> 01:14:33.640
That's great.

01:14:33.640 --> 01:14:34.600
That's wonderful.

01:14:34.600 --> 01:14:36.100
But that, again, is not enough.

01:14:36.100 --> 01:14:37.330
We believe there's more.

01:14:37.330 --> 01:14:39.370
If I'm going to
collaborate as a team,

01:14:39.370 --> 01:14:41.140
I need to have a
social dimension.

01:14:41.140 --> 01:14:43.160
I need to be able
to chat as a team.

01:14:43.160 --> 01:14:44.920
So if I create a
collaborative space,

01:14:44.920 --> 01:14:48.550
I also want to create a
collaborative talk environment

01:14:48.550 --> 01:14:50.530
where instead of
IM-ing to one or two

01:14:50.530 --> 01:14:53.530
people or just a small
team, what I can actually do

01:14:53.530 --> 01:14:56.500
is collaborate actively
with the entire team

01:14:56.500 --> 01:14:59.240
through the new Hangouts
Chat application.

01:14:59.240 --> 01:15:02.500
So picture setting up
a series of chat rooms

01:15:02.500 --> 01:15:05.510
on different topics,
on different projects,

01:15:05.510 --> 01:15:07.762
on different initiatives
within your organization,

01:15:07.762 --> 01:15:09.220
and then being able
to go into that

01:15:09.220 --> 01:15:11.680
and have persistence
over the conversation

01:15:11.680 --> 01:15:13.330
and be able to
seamlessly integrate

01:15:13.330 --> 01:15:16.480
all the content that's in Drive
with the conversations that

01:15:16.480 --> 01:15:18.820
are happening about
the content in Drive.

01:15:18.820 --> 01:15:22.210
So now just being able to
interact and collaborate

01:15:22.210 --> 01:15:26.340
actively is something that
we're bringing in Hangouts Chat.

01:15:26.340 --> 01:15:28.680
And then to complement
that, we also

01:15:28.680 --> 01:15:31.502
need to bring you a
meeting, a video meeting

01:15:31.502 --> 01:15:33.960
product that is going to meet
the demands of the enterprise

01:15:33.960 --> 01:15:35.160
use case.

01:15:35.160 --> 01:15:37.980
So being able to have the
ability to click a button

01:15:37.980 --> 01:15:42.930
and be able to initiate a
Hangout, a video collaboration

01:15:42.930 --> 01:15:44.610
amongst peers,
and collaborators,

01:15:44.610 --> 01:15:47.582
and partners instantaneously
is one dimension of it.

01:15:47.582 --> 01:15:49.290
But it's all the other
things that you've

01:15:49.290 --> 01:15:51.960
wanted for some time
in the Hangout product

01:15:51.960 --> 01:15:53.550
that are enterprise ready.

01:15:53.550 --> 01:15:56.370
So the ability to have,
for example, a one click

01:15:56.370 --> 01:15:58.380
access to where, when
I create a meeting,

01:15:58.380 --> 01:16:00.420
we automatically create
a conference bridge.

01:16:00.420 --> 01:16:04.950
We automatically can sense that
if I'm in a low bandwidth area

01:16:04.950 --> 01:16:07.050
using my mobile
phone, that I don't

01:16:07.050 --> 01:16:10.980
have to worry about connecting
through the video Hangout,

01:16:10.980 --> 01:16:13.560
but I can actually be
connected via a phone.

01:16:13.560 --> 01:16:17.220
Being able to record a session
so that I can persist it

01:16:17.220 --> 01:16:17.880
for later.

01:16:17.880 --> 01:16:20.307
How many times have you
gone into a session where

01:16:20.307 --> 01:16:22.140
you've been working
with people, but there's

01:16:22.140 --> 01:16:23.759
somebody who's on holiday?

01:16:23.759 --> 01:16:25.800
Or there's somebody who
is sick and can't make it

01:16:25.800 --> 01:16:26.670
into the office?

01:16:26.670 --> 01:16:29.730
But they don't want to lose
the context of the dialogue.

01:16:29.730 --> 01:16:32.040
They want to be able to
continue the conversation.

01:16:32.040 --> 01:16:34.560
So being able to record
the Hangout, we believe,

01:16:34.560 --> 01:16:36.115
is an important
dimension to this.

01:16:36.115 --> 01:16:38.490
There are many additional
features that I don't have time

01:16:38.490 --> 01:16:42.660
to talk about, but we believe
that Hangout Meet, right,

01:16:42.660 --> 01:16:44.760
is the ability to be able
to collaborate video.

01:16:47.568 --> 01:16:50.850
[MUSIC PLAYING]

01:16:50.850 --> 01:16:51.900
[BEGIN VIDEO PLAYBACK]

01:16:51.900 --> 01:16:55.280
- You're on Google and you're
enjoying the collaboration

01:16:55.280 --> 01:16:57.620
products-- mail,
calendar, contacts.

01:16:57.620 --> 01:17:00.200
However, you also have this
need for business process

01:17:00.200 --> 01:17:01.610
to be automated.

01:17:01.610 --> 01:17:04.610
- Our agency, they don't have
the money to do a full-fledged

01:17:04.610 --> 01:17:05.330
app.

01:17:05.330 --> 01:17:08.510
They just need something simple
that makes their life easier.

01:17:08.510 --> 01:17:09.950
Right now, we have
the Blue Form,

01:17:09.950 --> 01:17:11.408
because it's a blue
sheet of paper.

01:17:11.408 --> 01:17:13.486
- The Wyoming Flexible
Benefits Enrollment Plan.

01:17:13.486 --> 01:17:15.110
- You're filling it
out and signing it,

01:17:15.110 --> 01:17:16.730
and then they have
to data entry all

01:17:16.730 --> 01:17:21.070
that back in, 10,000
people, a lot of blue trees.

01:17:21.070 --> 01:17:23.060
- We were able to make
this in App Maker.

01:17:23.060 --> 01:17:24.830
- We showed it to
our HR department,

01:17:24.830 --> 01:17:27.440
and they were so excited.

01:17:27.440 --> 01:17:29.360
- Honestly, at first
I was very skeptical.

01:17:29.360 --> 01:17:32.090
It just seemed too easy,
like, oh yeah, I drag and drop

01:17:32.090 --> 01:17:33.049
a couple little things.

01:17:33.049 --> 01:17:33.673
What do I care?

01:17:33.673 --> 01:17:34.550
I'm a real developer.

01:17:34.550 --> 01:17:36.080
I don't use these
little gadgets.

01:17:36.080 --> 01:17:38.960
But as I got to use the tool
more, I was like wow, you know,

01:17:38.960 --> 01:17:42.180
this really can do
some pretty cool stuff.

01:17:42.180 --> 01:17:44.840
- I was able to develop a
relatively sophisticated app

01:17:44.840 --> 01:17:46.690
for login monitoring.

01:17:46.690 --> 01:17:50.210
From ideation all the way
through the final delivered app

01:17:50.210 --> 01:17:53.297
to our administrators for
them to use was five weeks.

01:17:53.297 --> 01:17:55.130
And that's just unheard
of in any other kind

01:17:55.130 --> 01:17:57.280
of product lifecycle.

01:17:57.280 --> 01:17:58.880
- Why App Maker?

01:17:58.880 --> 01:18:02.300
Because not everyone is me.

01:18:02.300 --> 01:18:06.290
I really like working deep down
in the code, working low level.

01:18:06.290 --> 01:18:08.300
The great thing
about App Maker is

01:18:08.300 --> 01:18:10.940
you don't need to have
that deep down knowledge.

01:18:10.940 --> 01:18:14.450
People were are able to make
these really snazzy looking

01:18:14.450 --> 01:18:17.930
applications that can be
used by an entire company.

01:18:17.930 --> 01:18:20.180
- I never pictured myself
developing anything.

01:18:20.180 --> 01:18:26.106
App Maker is an insanely awesome
way to solve a small problem.

01:18:26.106 --> 01:18:29.260
- App Maker makes my
job easier because I

01:18:29.260 --> 01:18:31.050
don't need multiple tools.

01:18:31.050 --> 01:18:35.800
I can just develop it
directly on App Maker.

01:18:35.800 --> 01:18:38.020
- One word to
describe App Maker?

01:18:38.020 --> 01:18:38.590
Simple.

01:18:38.590 --> 01:18:39.190
- Quick.

01:18:39.190 --> 01:18:39.810
- Flexible.

01:18:39.810 --> 01:18:40.590
- Versatile.

01:18:40.590 --> 01:18:41.290
- Empowerment.

01:18:41.290 --> 01:18:44.320
- One word to describe
App Maker, game changer.

01:18:51.084 --> 01:18:52.578
[END PLAYBACK]

01:18:52.578 --> 01:18:54.970
BILL HIPPENMEYER: So as part
of a collaboration platform,

01:18:54.970 --> 01:18:57.220
it's not enough just
to be able to infuse

01:18:57.220 --> 01:18:59.170
machine learning and
artificial intelligence

01:18:59.170 --> 01:19:01.900
to be able to allow you to work
and create the space you need.

01:19:01.900 --> 01:19:03.730
You also need a
platform that allows

01:19:03.730 --> 01:19:06.400
you to develop new
applications on top of,

01:19:06.400 --> 01:19:09.260
that's simple to use, easy
to be able to program,

01:19:09.260 --> 01:19:12.100
and does not require a lot
of deep code experience

01:19:12.100 --> 01:19:13.240
to be able to do that.

01:19:13.240 --> 01:19:16.930
So Google is committed, as
part of our overall platform,

01:19:16.930 --> 01:19:19.970
to providing you a development
environment, as well

01:19:19.970 --> 01:19:23.800
as a set of APIs, to be able to
do the back office integrations

01:19:23.800 --> 01:19:25.900
and to be able to
drive new collaborative

01:19:25.900 --> 01:19:29.200
experiences on top of a platform
that is built for connecting

01:19:29.200 --> 01:19:31.150
people and being
able to leverage

01:19:31.150 --> 01:19:32.930
the capabilities that we have.

01:19:32.930 --> 01:19:36.310
So not only do we have App Maker
as the environment with which

01:19:36.310 --> 01:19:38.290
you can build
applications, but we also

01:19:38.290 --> 01:19:41.500
are releasing a set of
APIs through the Sheets

01:19:41.500 --> 01:19:44.050
API and the Slides APIs,
which are the first ones

01:19:44.050 --> 01:19:46.630
to come to market, as
well as the ability

01:19:46.630 --> 01:19:49.450
to be able to build
applications that

01:19:49.450 --> 01:19:52.300
integrate with the other
components of the platform.

01:19:52.300 --> 01:19:54.760
So being able to do
things like Gmail add-ons,

01:19:54.760 --> 01:19:58.210
where how many times have
you been in an email--

01:19:58.210 --> 01:20:00.850
you know, we use email
every day for our to-do box.

01:20:00.850 --> 01:20:03.370
We use email to be able to
trigger the actions we're

01:20:03.370 --> 01:20:04.150
going to take.

01:20:04.150 --> 01:20:06.640
Why not be able to
integrate the back office

01:20:06.640 --> 01:20:09.100
into that experience
through the use of add-ons?

01:20:09.100 --> 01:20:11.440
So perhaps maybe
I have a CRM tool,

01:20:11.440 --> 01:20:14.680
and a customer sends me an
email about a particular ticket.

01:20:14.680 --> 01:20:18.820
Why can't I just launch the CRM
tool directly from the email,

01:20:18.820 --> 01:20:20.650
integrate it into
that experience,

01:20:20.650 --> 01:20:22.450
be able to go and
use the CRM tool

01:20:22.450 --> 01:20:24.970
to be able to solve the
problem, look up the customer,

01:20:24.970 --> 01:20:28.960
figure out what's going on, and
then be put back into the Gmail

01:20:28.960 --> 01:20:32.530
workflow to be able to respond
with information from that CRM

01:20:32.530 --> 01:20:36.430
system, in context, so they can
have a useful flow of activity

01:20:36.430 --> 01:20:37.970
going through that?

01:20:37.970 --> 01:20:40.210
So the idea here is
that we are bringing

01:20:40.210 --> 01:20:44.700
to market a set of
tools and capabilities

01:20:44.700 --> 01:20:48.390
that allow you to create
those transformative outcomes.

01:20:48.390 --> 01:20:51.180
You do that by
creating 10x ideas.

01:20:51.180 --> 01:20:54.030
From those 10x ideas,
the beginning of that

01:20:54.030 --> 01:20:55.950
is really the creative process.

01:20:55.950 --> 01:20:58.650
And the creative process
is catalyzed and fueled

01:20:58.650 --> 01:21:01.890
by your ability to
connect and collaborate.

01:21:01.890 --> 01:21:04.200
So what we'd like to
do next is I'd like

01:21:04.200 --> 01:21:06.870
to bring up the next speaker.

01:21:06.870 --> 01:21:11.050
Virginia Mateos, from GSS,
is one of our customers

01:21:11.050 --> 01:21:14.100
